{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e","id":1198537,"title":"Can non Zeniths become priests of the Unconquered Sun? (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-22T20:49:25-07:00","id":1198537,"title":"Can non Zeniths become priests of the Unconquered Sun? (2E)","content":"I am not sure if the situation has changed in 3E, but in 2E the UCS isn\u2019t really paying much attention to the prayers of humanity and the sort of relationship between a god and his priest is an intimate one. Can a mortal perhaps become the priest of Sol Invictus or is that going to just be a Zenith exclusive ability unless there is a plot development in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:01:47-07:00","id":1198543,"title":"","content":"I could imagine...<br /> <br /> A Dawn champion, who always spares his foes. He preaches by showing how mighty virtue is and how powerful solar faith is. He strikes his enemies down, only so that he can lift them up again. He tells them doubt and cynicism were their weakness and he has cut them out.<br /> <br /> A Twilight scholar, who studies and explores the infinite vastness of Creation and its secrets. She seeks to understand the beautiful mystery of Creation that the Unconquered Sun gave everything to protect. The more she learns, the more she understands the Sun.<br /> <br /> A Night magistrate, who punishes the wicked from the dark. Though he is a thing of shadows, he understands that even the Sun's shadow is righteous. He does not preach with mercy or lead with compassion. Instead he shocks the unbelievers into faith with fear.<br /> <br /> And an Eclipse politician, who seeks to bring everything into harmony. To her understanding, the Unconquered Sun's wisdom is infinite and only a perfect world can even begin to imagine it. To that goal, she wishes to reconnect and rebuild Creation so everyone is more ready to witness the Sun.<br /> <br /> ...though, I concede that the Zenith Caste is most likely to be the Sun's chief priests, since that's their shtick. Perhaps those above non-Zenith Priest of the Sun concepts don't have the same connection as the Zenith Caste has with the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3365-szp","name":"szp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3365_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:07:27-07:00","id":1198546,"title":"","content":"I believe there was the thing basically saying Zenith were default preists, but there's nothing preventing a person from being a priest regardless of any other detail. Granted the Zenith have perks for it, but it isn't exclusive to them. I think it was merit or something and Zenith were just listed as getting it by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:52:05-07:00","id":1198557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198546#post1198546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there was the thing basically saying Zenith were default preists, but there's nothing preventing a person from being a priest regardless of any other detail. Granted the Zenith have perks for it, but it isn't exclusive to them. I think it was merit or something and Zenith were just listed as getting it by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a merit to be a god\u2019s priest. I am trying to imagine a Zenith who wants to establish churches to the Sun that are complete with a legitimate priesthood that he has trained with Charms and can make sacrifices at the Temple Manses he designs and leaves behind. The problem is, the Sun seems to want the Solars to first prove Creation is worth his attention and likely can\u2019t give individual mortals his attention thanks to his addiction to the GoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 03-23-2018, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:29:23-07:00","id":1198563,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's still a working thaumaturgical ritual that the sun hears the prayer from, which if successful prompts him to instantly review the entirety of who you are as a person and every decision you've ever made. If he thinks you're a truly virtuous person with no other way out of the quandry you're petitioning him about, he'll send a Mouse of the Sun to advise you or subtly aid you. If he doesn't, he'll send a Mouse of the Sun to give you a disease which you can only keep from killing you through regular prayer, and which can only be permanently cured by begging the sun for mercy in person.<br /> <br /> If you were going to set up a priesthood of just enlightened terrestrials, or dragon kings, or something, meanwhile, you could use Eye of Heaven Style to ensure successful prayers - but I don't think the sun would be chill with that many disembodied hearts.<br /> <br /> Really, though, I think proper Priesthood to the sun is still a viable thing, if you're willing to deal with Immaculates. It's just, your prayers will be handled by the sun's secretary's secretary's secretary, instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 03-23-2018, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T02:58:23-07:00","id":1198597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e#post1198537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if the situation has changed in 3E,</div> </div> </div> </div> It has. In Ex3 Zeniths are not considered to be <i>inately </i>priests. Then again, <s><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">actually we don't have </span></span></span>prayer mechanics.</s> the prayer mechanics are hidden in the Pact With Ifrit Lord, and make no mention of priests (but no reason the merit cannot be reimported.) <div align=\"left\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e#post1198537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but in 2E the UCS isn\u2019t really paying much attention to the prayers of humanity and the sort of relationship between a god and his priest is an intimate one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not necessarily. Being a priest in exalted[Ex2] means/requires knowing how to pitch prayers and rites so that the god is slightly more likely to answer favourably. That doesn't require the god and priest to <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">actually </span></span></span></i><i>like </i>each other; though obviously that could surely help. But the cynical priest who flaters and conjols the god is entirely plausible. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e#post1198537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mortal perhaps become the priest of Sol Invictus or is that going to just be a Zenith exclusive ability unless there is a plot development in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Zenith perk, <i>shared </i>with No Moon Lunas, Midnight Abyssals, and all castes of Sidreals is to be considered <i>inately a </i>priest <i>irespective </i>of <i>actual </i>vocation. Nothing prevents anyone else from actually taking up the vocation if they have the motivation.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-23-2018, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T03:22:57-07:00","id":1198600,"title":"","content":"Please note: prayer mechanics get a mention in the Pact with an Ifrit Lord sorcery initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T05:23:06-07:00","id":1198615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e#post1198537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mortal perhaps become the priest of Sol Invictus or is that going to just be a Zenith exclusive ability unless there is a plot development in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt might be <i>Solar</i> exclusive, rather than Zenith, but I think either can work, leading in their own interesting directions. Even in Second Edition... I don't think there was anything that confirmed or denied the kind of prayer to the Sun that is the domain of a priest being proprietary to Solars. What would <i>you</i> want with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:34:51-07:00","id":1198644,"title":"","content":"Considering that the unconquered sun was the leading and thus most revered god before the usurpation it's hard to imagine him only having about 50 priests","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:51:39-07:00","id":1198655,"title":"","content":"Depends on him really. Maybe he's so important that he only considers Solars worthy to be his priests. Other worship leaders have to be stuck with being deacons, curates, etc, etc, etc...<br /> <br /> I mean, what even is a Priest of the UCS? A job anyone can do? A person the UCS listens to? Someone who's been ordained via apostolic succession?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:37:17-07:00","id":1198711,"title":"","content":"I see no issue with mortals, other solars castes, dragonbloods or whoever becoming a priest of the UCS. That said the Sun won't listen to their prayers anymore than he listens to any other prayers. I never got the impression that he listened to Zenith prayers either. Wether it's because he doesn't give a shit or wants the solars to prove themselves first, he doesn't listen to any prayers, wether they come from his priests or not. The bonus priests have is that they more easily can direct prayers towards the UCS... which then get redirected to his staff which delivers... a mixed bag of awnsers and miracles.<br /> <br /> The only time the UCS will interact with a solar, short of them breaching the jade pleasure dome, is when he exalts his Zeniths (and any other caste should he feel like sending them a message). Afterwards they're on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T16:12:26-07:00","id":1198878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198711#post1198711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no issue with mortals, other solars castes, dragonbloods or whoever becoming a priest of the UCS. That said the Sun won't listen to their prayers anymore than he listens to any other prayers. I never got the impression that he listened to Zenith prayers either. Wether it's because he doesn't give a shit or wants the solars to prove themselves first, he doesn't listen to any prayers, wether they come from his priests or not. The bonus priests have is that they more easily can direct prayers towards the UCS... which then get redirected to his staff which delivers... a mixed bag of awnsers and miracles.<br /> <br /> The only time the UCS will interact with a solar, short of them breaching the jade pleasure dome, is when he exalts his Zeniths (and any other caste should he feel like sending them a message). Afterwards they're on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This pretty much sums up my thoughts. The entirety of our real world clergy are priests of their respective deities despite a complete inaction of the divine being's part. Just means the priest is gonna attribute random providence to divine intervention with the added bonus of maybe, some day, doing something awesome enough that they pay attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T03:51:23-07:00","id":1198994,"title":"","content":"Considering that the UCS is one of the Incarnae, and the Immaculate religion gives ALL gods due reverence at the correct times, I'd say, as others have, that he'd have to be getting prayers regularly. And further considering his stated position as the preeminent Incarnae, he probably has actively dedicated temples on and around the Realm and all controlled Satrapies, with clergy dedicated just to his worship. Add to that the relative ease of getting the &quot;Priest&quot; Merit, and there are certainly thousands of dedicated priests to the Unconquered Sun. Mostly Mortals, but still probably a quite a few DBs, some of whom would actually be Dynasts doing their actual monkish jobs. Probably as a rota, just to keep things from getting... difficult.<br /> <br /> It's just easier for Zeniths, by dint of Creation's Rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4623-onigato","name":"Onigato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T05:39:48-07:00","id":1199010,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198644#post1198644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the unconquered sun was the leading and thus most revered god before the usurpation it's hard to imagine him only having about 50 priests</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThere have been religious systems in which the higher a god is, the more exclusive their worship becomes; where it being the province of a specific class or caste, right up to the point of being limited to the monarch, is a sign of prestige, or recognition that there are few that are worthy to pray directly to them or perform the appropriate rites to honour them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIt depends on whether or not one sees the worship of the Unconquered Sun as a populist religion.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bMind, considering the flexibility of the Cult Merit as demonstrated by the sum of every spirit's Cult depicted in the corebook, I interpret it as including the idea that when you're the local absolute monarch, you're empowered to pray on behalf of your dominion; if the Scarlet Empress ever performed rites to a god in her function as monarch and shogun of the Realm, that right there is Cult 5 even if that worship is forbidden to every other person in the Realm.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198711#post1198711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never got the impression that he listened to Zenith prayers either.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Games of Divinity depicted the Unconquered Sun as being enthusiastically involved with the Solars and the Realm.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThere's a reason that the high priest invoking his name in vain was a major breaking point.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198878#post1198878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entirety of our real world clergy are priests of their respective deities despite a complete inaction of the divine being's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that they'd see it that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T05:56:02-07:00","id":1199013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199010#post1199010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bMind, considering the flexibility of the Cult Merit as demonstrated by the sum of every spirit's Cult depicted in the corebook, I interpret it as including the idea that when you're the local absolute monarch, you're empowered to pray on behalf of your dominion; if the Scarlet Empress ever performed rites to a god in her function as monarch and shogun of the Realm, that right there is Cult 5 even if that worship is forbidden to every other person in the Realm.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I... personally did not get that impression at all. I'd have to reread the Cult merit to see where you are coming from, but humans have been made as prayer machines. I don't think one machine is more efficient at prayer just because they hold technical soverignty over other mortals... all the mortals have to pray. The Hierophant usually lead huge congressions himself and didn't pray alone in his sanctum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Games of Divinity depicted the Unconquered Sun as being enthusiastically involved with the Solars and the Realm.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThere's a reason that the high priest invoking his name in vain was a major breaking point.</span></span></span></div><br /> </div> </div> </div>Well aside from this being specifically about 2e, not 1e, I was mostly speaking about the situation in the normal perceived timeframe. During the majority of the first age (most of the pre usurpation age) you are correct, UCS did pay attention. But not anymore. The point is wether you can pray efficiently to him or not (nothing else is the base priest merit. The 7 dot version may be more involved, but I doubt anyone has that for Sol at the moment because he doesn't give a shit) doesn't mean Sol actually listens to or cares about your prayers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T06:55:15-07:00","id":1199029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199013#post1199013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to reread the Cult merit to see where you are coming from</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't read the Merit, read the spirit write-ups in the Antagonists chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">humans have been made as prayer machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about things in the context of Second Edition, this was a thing that those books said. I nevertheless dispute the value of it as a fact of the setting for a number of reasons regarding its implications and purpose, and so do not give it serious consideration in my assessment of relations between mortals and divinities.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think one machine is more efficient at prayer just because they hold technical soverignty over other mortals... all the mortals have to pray.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Technical</i> sovereignty?<br /> <br /> \u200bSecond Edition depicted the Empress' ownership of the Blessed Isle as a metaphysical thing to the point where the Ebon Dragon could use marriage to her as a way of escaping Malfeas.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe terminology that you're employing here is among the reasons that I would disdain the &quot;mortals were made to be prayer batteries&quot; thing, by the way; when it comes to something like a cult, I care a lot more about cultural conventions, nuances in relationships and general diverse approaches, rather than finding the one technical way that it all works and standardising things to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well aside from this being specifically about 2e, not 1e, I was mostly speaking about the situation in the normal perceived timeframe. During the majority of the first age (most of the pre usurpation age) you are correct, UCS did pay attention. But not anymore. The point is wether you can pray efficiently to him or not (nothing else is the base priest merit. The 7 dot version may be more involved, but I doubt anyone has that for Sol at the moment because he doesn't give a shit) doesn't mean Sol actually listens to or cares about your prayers.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt speaks to having a capacity to care that can be developed in the course of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:04:10-07:00","id":1199033,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'll not awnser in detail to the rest in order not to derail the thread. I think the two of us simply disagree in a few areas. Personally I liked 2es &quot;scientific&quot; approach to the metaphysical underpinnings of creation, which in my mind doesn't have to exclude more esoteric relations. For example scarlet could likely redirect the faith people have in her towards a divinity via prayers, giving her alot of oomph. But say an unloved, newly established tyrant in one of the hundred kingdoms prays only with his own voice, no matter how big his domain is (unless he forces people for worship to him/in his name/whatever).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199029#post1199029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bIt speaks to having a capacity to care that can be developed in the course of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically true and never disputed. The problem being of course that Sol has effectivly blindfolded and deafened himself, deliberatly not taking notice of creation and people praying to him. He could be persuaded to care again... but that is rather hard when it is essentially impossible to interact with him in the first place. I'd certainly be a worthy goal for a whole chronicle about a devout Zenith who wishes to bring creation back into UCS good graces.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:08:41-07:00","id":1199036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onigato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1198994#post1198994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the UCS is one of the Incarnae, and the Immaculate religion gives ALL gods due reverence at the correct times, I'd say, as others have, that he'd have to be getting prayers regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is an not minor distinction between prayers delivering <i>reverence</i>, and prayers delivering <i>requests. </i>Particularly those with <i>some </i>expectation of being considered. The Immaculate Order <i>rather </i>discourages the later from being attempted, especially by mortals (even their mortal monks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 03-24-2018, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:37:42-07:00","id":1199089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199010#post1199010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that they'd see it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they don't see it that way. That's my point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:53:16-07:00","id":1199097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199089#post1199089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course they don't see it that way. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is that in Exalted, the standards for recognising divine intervention remain the same, despite the more overt existence of gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:25:34-07:00","id":1199106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199089#post1199089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they don't see it that way. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that in Exalted, to a large degree, prayer and worship are more like business arrangements than anything else. If a town prays to some god, and that god never intervenes or helps them, it's very likely the town will eventually start praying to a god who will intervene. &quot;God X hasn't sent us rain in five years even though we keep praying to him and now we're dying. Let's try praying to Gods A, B, C, D and E and see if any of them will give us water instead.&quot; It's much easier in Exalted to shop around for gods to pray to (heck, depending on the location it's entirely possible to meet or even have a chat with a god) so people are generally going to be more likely to worship gods who take an active interest in the world than those who ignore them and their problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:54:33-07:00","id":1199116,"title":"","content":"To the extent that the business arrangement side of it matters, it's worth remembering the general idea of worship because you specifically <i>don't</i> want a god to intervene.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough that doesn't matter as such with the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:05:33-07:00","id":1199121,"title":"","content":"Although I do get great amusement from the idea of people feverishly praying that the sun does not send his mice to them after several really bad experiences with the mice finding the town wanting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:20:51-07:00","id":1199122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199116#post1199116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the extent that the business arrangement side of it matters, it's worth remembering the general idea of worship because you specifically <i>don't</i> want a god to intervene.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough that doesn't matter as such with the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe in his aspect of a war deity?<br /> I also think it's important to note that divine intervention might be a less than obvious source. UCS might have victories attributed to him, or a bumper harvest, or other phenomona that are in fact unrelated to him. Incarnae priests, where they exist, might also tend towards the more mystical &quot;the UCS sustains all the world&quot; traditions, then the temple traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:20:51-07:00","id":1199123,"title":"","content":"Double post. I'd note real quick that praying to _not_ get that nasty plauge might have been a thing? Or in search of ultimate justice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:50:02-07:00","id":1199134,"title":"","content":"Prayer to the Unconquered Sun has been distinctly absent through most of Creation in the last few centuries, evidently with a lack of retribution. That could be considered part of the reason why that worship has been described as largely forgotten.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you stop praying to your local rain deity because he's not been making it rain to your benefit, and switch to a nearby harvest god, there are many cases in which you should hope that your new god can beat your old one in a fight, otherwise you might soon find yourself with more rain than you can stomach.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf we're going by Second Edition, that was one that was <i>distinctly</i> emphatic on that point. Probably too much, but there you go.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's often a transactional element to prayer in Creation, but in much of the world, it isn't a buyer's market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T22:09:13-07:00","id":1199301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1198537-can-non-zeniths-become-priests-of-the-unconquered-sun-2e?p=1199106#post1199106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that in Exalted, to a large degree, prayer and worship are more like business arrangements than anything else. If a town prays to some god, and that god never intervenes or helps them, it's very likely the town will eventually start praying to a god who will intervene. &quot;God X hasn't sent us rain in five years even though we keep praying to him and now we're dying. Let's try praying to Gods A, B, C, D and E and see if any of them will give us water instead.&quot; It's much easier in Exalted to shop around for gods to pray to (heck, depending on the location it's entirely possible to meet or even have a chat with a god) so people are generally going to be more likely to worship gods who take an active interest in the world than those who ignore them and their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were the case, the majority of Celestial gods would have no cults. Most of them are far too corrupt and self- important to do anything resembling divine intervention on behalf of even a fraction of the people within their sphere of influence.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that even with real gods, most people are never going to see them. Even elementals are rare enough that the default reaction is to fall on your knees and pray while someone runs for the local monk or shaman. People might not even be aware that there are other gods. The local lame-ass wolf god might have convinced everyone in the valley that all the other spirits work for him, so there is no point in switching worship. He might have legitimately beat up all the other valley gods and made himself king-god and there really are no other other options.<br /> <br /> Most people in Creation have to take what they are given as far as gods go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}